        "pillar_nature": {
          "type": "pillar",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Nature",
            "body": "<p>The base of every product is cold-pressed organic and plant oils, chosen for the compounds that refining tends to strip away: carotenoids, tocopherols, phytosterols and phenolics. We add no synthetic fragrance, and nothing hides behind a \"parfum\" catch-all. The range uses one essential oil, vetiver, at a tenth of a percent, named on every label. Bladderwrack ties the range to where it is made. It is the same Atlantic seaweed that grows on the rocks below Welcombe, used as a cold infusion in sunflower oil made in the UK.</p>",
            "link_label": "How we formulate",
            "link_url": "/pages/how-we-formulate"
          }
        },
        "pillar_science": {
          "type": "pillar",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Science",
            "body": "<p>Current research treats skin as an ecosystem, and so do we. The decision with the strongest evidence behind it is the product's pH. Ours is slightly acidic (pH 5 to 5.5), close to the pH of healthy skin, which the skin's resident microbes prefer. A plant prebiotic, inulin, feeds beneficial skin bacteria in laboratory studies, and nothing in the formula is there to strip them away.</p>",
            "inset": "<p>Biotaderm reviews the published science. It does not conduct it. So we credit the research, never ourselves, and claim only what the evidence supports.</p>",
            "link_label": "How we handle evidence",
            "link_url": "/pages/how-we-handle-evidence"
          }
        },
        "pillar_ethics": {
          "type": "pillar",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Ethics",
            "body": "<p>Every ingredient is published with its exact percentage, most abundant first, with a plain-English name beside each INCI name. That is unusual in a category that treats formulas as trade secrets. It sits alongside recyclable aluminium bottles, a small range where each product has to earn its place, and a business working toward B Corp certification.</p>",
            "link_label": "Our ethics",
            "link_url": "/pages/our-ethics"
          }
        },
